{"id": "EUVD-2026-86150", "enisaUuid": "4a3cfb95-7272-36a2-8664-b31bcee53895", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nstaging: octeon: add missing napi_disable in cvm_oct_rx_shutdown\n\ncvm_oct_rx_shutdown calls free_irq and netif_napi_del without\ndisabling the napi instance first. As the free_irq only waits\nfor completion of hard interrupt handlers, the napi poll\nfunction could still be active. If cvm_oct_remove proceeds to\nfree the plat structure (which holds the NAPI instances), the\nactive poll function will access freed memory, resulting in a\nuse-after-free crash.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:52:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:32", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/158389d7af04bbf0664d91c2ce31fcc9eeace1eb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c124049c3a7006fd6caf629139a5722610bbffb4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98f9036b2254c928cb44da0c77dba38f66f7d8f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b38fbd68cc36b4f478a1e3cfc169b8616ae1337d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89f9f433271fad9351de6a3c713b45b2cfb23e4a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2243ffaac14cc3639b5b32a371aac37f96ee554", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0a9a8586a63fda49e61a6b83360feac2a60d898"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7ppg-qghw-hg2g", "CVE-2026-93278"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "110e31a0-5cee-3c0d-aa83-f6fdd7a87e2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3368c784bcf77124aaf39372e627016c36bd4472 <98f9036b2254c928cb44da0c77dba38f66f7d8f1"}, {"id": "11cd3785-73aa-3ad9-b83b-92b81010760b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3368c784bcf77124aaf39372e627016c36bd4472 <c0a9a8586a63fda49e61a6b83360feac2a60d898"}, {"id": "2fa12e64-9c7e-3823-8dff-569ed21682d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "30fe94a5-70fa-3dae-8d57-cee0feaa9f4e", "produ